  "term": "polygenic trait",
  "definition": "A polygenic trait is a characteristic that is strongly influenced by genetic background through many genetic contributions rather than a single factor. The packet also indicates that such traits can be shaped by environmental and behavioral influences, as illustrated by body mass index.",
